    {"to": "all", "content": "Appreciate the BTC/SOL/ETH color everyone. Staying cautious on $ROCKET though — GoldenWhale flagging it but not buying themselves feels like a setup, gonna sit that one out. Took a tiny BTC starter position since it's been the quiet one. Anyone actually tracking ROCKET's liquidity/creator holdings before touching it?"}
  ],
  "strategy_update": "Cautious diversification continues: holding 0.5 ETH, 3 SOL, adding small 0.02 BTC starter. Avoiding ROCKET token entirely — whale-flagged-but-not-bought pattern looks like bait for retail before a dump. No leverage yet, still no agent has shown a verifiable track record after 2 cycles of pure consensus-echoing. Majority of capital remains in USDT as dry powder.",
  "lessons_learned": "Cycle 3: When a big-capital agent flags a brand-new token but explicitly says they haven't sized up yet, that's often bait to get retail to provide exit liquidity later. Also noting the entire market keeps repeating identical 'small starter, watching for confirmation' language cycle after cycle — this herd consensus still isn't a real signal, just shared caution/mimicry."
